The package qpOASES

  https://github.com/coin-or/qpOASES

is not included as part of GALAHAD, but may be
called optionally from GALAHAD's ubersolver QP package.

GALAHAD relies on an environment variable,
and if qpOASES has not been installed, these 
are set by default as

  QPOASES = -lgalahad_qpoases

This allows GALAHAD to function, but any attempt
to use qpOASES will result in an error return code.

If you wish to use qpOASES ...

1. Download qpOASES via git to a suitable location via

    git clone https://github.com/coin-or/qpOASES

  and then move into the qpOASES directory using

     cd ./qpOASES

   we shall refer to this through the shell variable $qpOASES

2. Install the package into a suitable subdirectory using make

   This is appropriate for default GALAHAD interactions, but
   -D__USE_SINGLE_PRECISION__ and -D__USE_LONG_INTEGERS__ change
   from double- to single-precision reals and 64- rather than 32-bit
   integers
   
   You can use other compilers by, e.g., resetting them prior to
   the first call, e.g. (in the bash shell)

      CC=icx CXX=icpx FC=ifx make ....
   
   On Windows systems, you may need to change the
     typedef long definitions to typedef int64_t
   in $qpOASES/interfaces/c/qpOASES_wrapper.h to make sure
   that 64-bit integers really are 64 bits long!

3. Now call GALAHAD with the envirnment variables

      QPOASES_DIR = $(qpOASES)
      QPOASES = -lqpoases_fortran -lgalahad \
          $(QPOASES_DIR)/bin/libqpOASES.a -lstdc++

